===Defensive skills===
====Hitpoints====
[[Hitpoints]] is the skill that determines the maximum health of a player or NPC. When a player or NPC's health reaches zero they die. As such the Hitpoints skill plays an important role in combat. There are various methods of adjusting a player's hitpoints:

* Hitpoints regenerate at the rate of 1 Hitpoint per minute passively; Certain [[Hitpoints#Regeneration|prayers and equipment]] can speed  this effect up.

* Hitpoints are primarily restored through the use of [[food]] and [[potions]]. Some [[Magic]] is also be used, such as [[blood spells]] , [[Heal Other|the Heal Other spell]], or the passive effect of the [[Sanguinesti staff]]. There are roundabout methods of healing, including healing others through [[Butterfly (Hunter)|butterflies]] and Magic, or going to an [[NPC]] for healing, such as a [[monk]], but these methods are often ineffective and uncommon.
* It is possible to temporarily boost a player's health past their current maximum Hitpoints through the use of certain [[Hitpoints#Temporary boosts|foods, potions, and equipment]].

====Defence====
[[Defence]] is another skill which plays an active role in nearly all combat situations. Defence as a skill doesn't directly reduce the damage taken per hit; Instead, it causes the attacker to be more likely to miss their attack. In this way, Defence could be equated to "evasiveness". 

=====Player magic defence=====
While [[Defence]] is responsible for reducing the accuracy of most hits, it is only 30% effective against [[Magic]] [[spells]]. Instead, 70% of the reduction of accuracy for a spell is determined by the player's own Magic level.

=====Monster magic defence=====
[[Monster]] magic defence is not affected by their Defence level, only Magic level and Magic defence bonus. See [[Magic]].

===Prayer===
[[Prayer]], the final combat skill. Each Prayer level grants an additional maximum "prayer point" which are used to activate temporary passive boosts that the player unlocks as they increase their Prayer skill ([[Prayer scroll|or receive as drops from certain monsters]]). Prayer effects include increasing [[stat]]s while active, [[Protect Item|protecting items]] upon [[death]], providing increased [[Hitpoints]] regeneration, and even the ability to [[Protection prayers|prevent all incoming damage]]. While prayers are active, the player's [[Prayer points]] are slowly drained at a rate dependent on both the type of prayer and any prayer bonuses provided by equipment, and prayers can no longer be used when all prayer points have been drained. Unlike Hitpoints, prayer points do not regenerate over time (outside of the [[Demonic Ruins]]) and can only be restored by praying at an altar, consuming potions, or using certain [[Special attacks]].

===Sailing===
{{main|Boat combat}}
Combat with monsters in the sea while the player is on a [[boat]] has some additional mechanics:
* Boats have a unique [[boat armour|armour]] mechanic and take damage in place of the player,
* [[Cannons]] can be manned by [[crewmates]], and if so their accuracy is dictated by the player's [[Sailing]] level,
* <!--Damage the player deals with weapons that are not cannons is significantly reduced, and (this was patched)-->Melee weapons outside of [[salamanders]] cannot be used.

==Other factors==
While skills are an important aspect of Combat, damage done and received is mostly determined by external traits, and there is a multitude of other factors that contribute to the fight.

===Armour and weaponry===
Generally, armour boosts a player's defensive capabilities by reducing the accuracy of incoming attacks, and weaponry boosts a player's offensive capabilities. However, armour may also provide offensive bonuses, and weapons usually provide minor defensive bonuses. For maximum effectiveness, players should use the best equipment available to them, since bonuses provided by equipment are at least as important as levels in combat skills.

=====Damage absorption=====
The [[Elysian spirit shield]], [[Dinh's bulwark]], and [[Justiciar armour]] set effects are currently the only pieces of armour that provide general damage absorption abilities. Certain shields and potions can reduce the damage taken from [[Dragonfire]] and [[Icy breath]], and the [[Neitiznot shield]] reduces damage taken from [[Ice troll female|ice troll females]] and [[Thrower Troll|thrower trolls]].

===Skill boosts===
Stat increases are available to anybody through the use of [[potions]] and certain [[food]] items. Through skill boosts, one can temporarily increase a combat statistic to a higher level. These boosts can cause a player's combat stats to exceed the cap of 99.

===Special attacks===
[[Special attack]]s are specific to some [[weapon]]s that a player can wield. Special attacks consume a set percentage of the special attack bar in exchange for an effect specific to the weapon, which may include extra damage, additional hits, stat drains, and many others.

===Attack speed===
All weapons have a specific [[Attack speed|speed]], which determines the interval between successive hits. Fast weapons tend not to be as accurate or powerful as their counterparts. Fast, inaccurate weapons are ideal against enemies with low Defence, while slower, more accurate weapons fare better against enemies with high Defence.

